# GNOME desktop (SDD §11). Bluefin-like UX, independently maintained.

gnome-shell

# Rule 11: provisioning that needs a user account (group membership, Homebrew)
# can only run AFTER gnome-initial-setup creates it — i.e. once the user is
# already looking at their desktop. The boot splash cannot cover that phase, so
# without a notification the machine silently downloads for several minutes and
# looks broken. Used by ik-os-homebrew and ik-os-user-groups.
libnotify-bin
# The progress window ik-os-provisioning-monitor draws while Homebrew and the
# company Brewfile install after first login. zenity's stdin protocol means no
# GTK code of ours; measured against the image's dpkg database this and
# zenity-common are the only two packages it adds.
zenity
gnome-session
gdm3
gnome-initial-setup             # SDD §36/§37 — creates the first user account on
                                # first boot. The image ships no accounts and a
                                # locked root (SDD §27), so without this GDM comes
                                # up with nothing to log in as.
gnome-control-center            # printer UI required by SDD §23
gnome-settings-daemon
gnome-terminal
nautilus
gnome-text-editor
gnome-disk-utility
# No gnome-system-monitor either: Mission Center replaces it as a Flatpak.
# Its two privileged helpers do have to live here, though: a sandboxed app
# cannot give a binary file capabilities, and cannot write them to a read-only
# /usr afterwards (docs/adr/0013-mission-center-host-helpers.md).
nethogs                         # per-process bandwidth; needs file capabilities
lm-sensors                      # sensors-detect, which the app's setup probes for
# No gnome-software. The graphical app store is Bazaar, installed as a Flatpak
# (config/desktop/system-flatpaks.list) — a Flatpak-native store for a
# Flatpak-first desktop (SDD §15, §54), and one less GUI stack in the immutable
# image.
xdg-desktop-portal
xdg-desktop-portal-gnome
xdg-user-dirs-gtk
dconf-cli                       # required to compile desktop/gnome/dconf at build time
libglib2.0-bin                  # gsettings, used to validate the dconf keys at build time
plymouth
plymouth-themes                 # branding watermark (branding/plymouth)
fonts-cantarell
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
wireplumber
power-profiles-daemon
gnome-shell-extension-manager   # lets developers manage their own extensions (SDD §53)

# Anthropic's first-party package, from their own signed APT repository
# (config/apt/claude-desktop.sources). Not in Debian and not on Flathub, so
# SDD §54's Flatpak route does not apply — see docs/adr/0007-claude-desktop.md.
claude-desktop

